course: dictionary
lesson: 15316
title: Adverbs that show how
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An adverb tells you how, when or where something happens. Smilingly is an adverb: it tells you how someone speaks or acts. «"Good morning," said Mrs Patel smilingly as she opened the door.» The word smilingly tells you her voice and face were friendly.
explain: Look at the word's ending. Smilingly ends in -ly, and many adverbs do. Ask yourself: how did they do it? «The waiter smilingly brought us our soup.» How did he bring the soup? With a smile, in a friendly way.
explain: Sometimes a character smiles while hiding a feeling. «"I'm fine," she said smilingly, but her hands were shaking.» The word smilingly shows how she spoke, but her shaking hands show she may be nervous. Read the words around smilingly to see whether the smile is honest.
fact: Smilingly means while smiling, in a smiling and friendly way.
fact: Smilingly is an adverb, because it tells how someone speaks or acts.
fact: Writers use smilingly to show a character is happy, friendly or politely pleased.
fact: A character can speak smilingly while hiding what they really feel.
fact: A good check is to swap in «in a friendly way» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «Tom handed back the book smilingly.» How did Tom hand back the book? | Crossly and in a hurry | Without looking up | Very quietly and slowly | *In a smiling, friendly way
exercise: «"Yes, of course," said Ana smilingly, though she did not want to go.» Find and copy the adverb. | *smilingly | said | course | Yes
exercise: Why might a character speak smilingly while hiding their feelings? | To show they are very tired | To tell everyone they are lost | *To seem friendly, even though they feel differently | Lost in thought
test: «The shopkeeper greeted us smilingly.» What does smilingly mean? | *In a smiling, friendly way | Without any words | Very slowly | Angrily and loudly
test: Which word is the adverb in «He answered smilingly and waved goodbye»? | *smilingly | goodbye | answered | waved
exam: «She smilingly offered me a seat, but her eyes looked worried.» What does smilingly suggest, and what might the worried eyes show? | Sleepy and bored with the visit | Lost, and looking for the door | Angry and rude, because she is shouting | *Polite and friendly on the surface, though she may feel differently
